{"ok":true,"total":3,"succeeded":3,"failed":0,"concurrency":3,"durationMs":56432,"results":[{"id":"1-paper-A","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-min/1-paper-A.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ce-d0ea-72f3-8612-a1f8aba9b747/exec-290d7db6-9c47-4fa7-b0f1-31b2711938a1.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image, a wide 16:9 desktop video game screenshot for a premium minimalist strategy board game titled “War Table.” Show the whole board mid-game: a recognizable world map including the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into plausible territories owned by four players. Paper-and-ink art direction: warm off-white paper ground #f7f3ea with only the faintest natural paper grain; ocean remains mostly empty paper with just a few faint horizontal ink strokes; one faint ink-wash mountain ridge at the far edge is the only scenic decoration. Use one consistent fine line weight for every coastline and internal territory border, rendered in soft charcoal ink. Territory ownership is conveyed only by very pale, low-saturation watercolor washes contained within territories: muted vermilion, dusty indigo, soft ochre, and sage. Put exactly one gameplay mark in each territory: a small readable number in an elegant high-contrast serif, centered inside a thin hairline circle. Do not add any other marks inside territories. One territory is selected using a slightly stronger outline, with one fine curved attack arrow pointing to a neighboring territory. Use gold only for hairline accents and the single active UI element. Recurring motif: restrained small ring ornaments with a center dot.\n\nTypography throughout uses one elegant high-contrast serif similar to Cormorant Garamond, in deep navy. The title “War Table” should be subtle and refined. Maintain extreme restraint, generous negative space, and one cohesive premium-app design system. No soldier figures, pieces, flags, seals, coats of arms, fake characters, icons beyond the ring-and-dot motif, decorative clutter, or watermark.\n\nAt the bottom, create a quiet generous UI area separated from the map by one thin gold hairline rule with a small ring-and-center-dot ornament exactly at its center. Include a soft rounded-pill segmented control with the exact readable labels “Place   Attack   Fortify   End turn”; “Attack” is the single active segment, filled with a soft muted gold-toned color. Include one small separate button labeled “Blitz.” Ensure labels are correctly spelled and highly readable. Calm editorial composition, premium material feel, delicate ink and watercolor, high detail, crisp interface, balanced desktop screenshot, straight-on view, no perspective distortion.","bytes":2152299,"durationMs":54542,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ce-d0ea-72f3-8612-a1f8aba9b747"},{"id":"1-paper-C","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-min/1-paper-C.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ce-cfb9-70e3-a2db-07c17737e39d/exec-b927f754-3b2b-4676-9d85-b6f218568dc6.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image, a tall portrait 9:19.5 smartphone video game screenshot for a game titled “War Table.”\n\nArt direction: minimalist, cohesive, calm world-conquest strategy board game in the spirit of classic Risk, rendered as premium paper-and-ink editorial design. Warm off-white paper ground (#f7f3ea) with extremely faint natural paper grain. The recognizable world map fills most of the screen while preserving generous negative space: the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into plausible game territories owned by four players. Use exactly one consistent fine soft charcoal-ink line weight for every coastline and every internal territory border. Ocean remains mostly empty paper, with only a few very faint horizontal ink strokes. At the far outer edge, include one barely visible ink-wash mountain ridge as the only scenic decoration.\n\nTerritory ownership must be shown only by very pale, low-saturation watercolor washes contained within territories: muted vermilion, dusty indigo, soft ochre, and sage. Exactly one mark per territory: a small readable integer set in an elegant high-contrast serif, centered inside a thin hairline circle. No territory may contain any other icon or mark. Use deep navy for all text. Gold appears only in hairline accents and on the single active UI element. Small ring ornaments with one center dot are the sole recurring motif.\n\nUI composition: four tiny player color dots with small counts arranged neatly at the top. Include the understated title “War Table” if space permits, in the same elegant serif. Along the bottom, one soft rounded pill control containing the four readable labels “Place   Attack   Fortify   End”; make “Attack” the single active element using restrained gold hairline treatment. Add one separate compact “Blitz” button, also restrained and clearly readable, but do not make it compete with the active Attack state. All interface text uses one elegant high-contrast serif typeface similar to Cormorant Garamond. The map, counts, labels, and buttons must be crisp, coherent, premium, balanced, and genuinely readable at phone scale.\n\nExtreme restraint. Unified design system. No soldier figures, armies, figurines, flags, shields, seals, crowns, fake characters, fantasy glyphs, decorative frames, scenery clutter, gradients, glossy effects, photorealistic devices, hands, watermark, logo watermark, or extra text. Show only the flat full-screen app screenshot, not a phone mockup. High detail, polished final raster artwork.","bytes":2276630,"durationMs":50775,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ce-cfb9-70e3-a2db-07c17737e39d"},{"id":"2-night-A","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-min/2-night-A.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ce-d012-7fd2-af34-2e15b4c2cc10/exec-9fcb4a8c-3706-4a26-852b-8b05fe308026.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image: a minimalist, cohesive premium video game screenshot titled \"War Table\", a calm world-conquest strategy board game in the spirit of classic Risk. Wide 16:9 desktop view showing the whole board mid-game.\n\nUse a recognizable world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into plausible territories owned by four players. Apply extreme restraint and generous negative space. Use exactly one consistent thin line weight for every coastline and internal border. Show ownership only through soft, low-saturation watercolor washes contained inside territories: muted coral, slate blue, pale gold, and sage, softly luminous against the dark ground. Put exactly one gameplay mark in each territory: a small readable troop number in an elegant high-contrast serif, centered inside a delicate hairline circle. No other mark inside territories.\n\nNight-ink visual system: deep navy ground #1b2230 with subtle fine grain; thin warm-ivory coastlines and borders; luminous restrained territory tinting; ivory serif typography throughout, like Cormorant Garamond; gold used only for hairline accents and the single active element. Small ring ornaments with a center dot are the sole recurring decorative motif. Fine dotted gold sea routes.\n\nOne territory is selected using a subtly stronger gold outline, with one fine curved gold attack arrow pointing to an adjacent territory. The result should remain calm and uncluttered.\n\nAt the bottom, reserve a quiet spacious UI area. Separate it from the map with a thin gold hairline rule and a small centered ring ornament containing a dot. Include a soft rounded-pill segmented control with exactly these labels, spelled correctly and in this order: \"Place   Attack   Fortify   End turn\". Make only \"Attack\" the active filled segment in a soft muted color with a restrained gold accent. Add one small button labeled \"Blitz\". Keep everything aligned, legible, sparse, and part of one coherent premium app design system.\n\nNo soldier figures, miniatures, flags, seals, fake characters, extra icons, banners, decorative scenery, clutter, bevels, loud gradients, excessive glow, watermark, logo, or extra text. High detail, readable, elegant, quiet, like a refined star chart.","bytes":2311854,"durationMs":56290,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ce-d012-7fd2-af34-2e15b4c2cc10"}]}
